{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"stronglyConnectedComponents"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity10ComponentsV","text":"Components"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"title":"stronglyConnectedComponents()","modules":[{"name":"Connectivity","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Connectivity\/StronglyConnectedComponents.swift#L136","fileName":"StronglyConnectedComponents.swift"},"role":"symbol","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","roleHeading":"Instance Method","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P12ConnectivityE27stronglyConnectedComponentsAD0G0VyxGyF","symbolKind":"method"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The strongly connected components: maximal sets of vertices each reaching every other."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Tarjan’s algorithm, iterative, O(V + E)."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/stronglyConnectedComponents()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/stronglyconnectedcomponents()"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"stronglyConnectedComponents","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity10ComponentsV","text":"Components","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Components are in the order Tarjan’s algorithm completes them, on a depth-first search"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with roots in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order and successors in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" order (the order of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"NetworkX, petgraph and Boost). That is a reverse topological order of the condensation:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every edge between components goes from a later component to an earlier one, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reversed()"},{"type":"text","text":" lists the components with every edge going forward. Each component lists its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each component’s first vertex is its earliest in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":", so on a graph whose vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"positions are insertion order ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StableDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"), one sort puts the components in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"insertion order:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let inInsertionOrder = graph.stronglyConnectedComponents().sorted { graph.vertices.firstIndex(of: $0.first!)! < graph.vertices.firstIndex(of: $1.first!)! }"]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P","kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedGraph"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","title":"DirectedGraph","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedGraph"}],"abstract":[]},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols","role":"collection","abstract":[],"title":"GraphProtocols","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/Components":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Components","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Components","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A partition of a graph’s vertices into components, in a documented order: a collection of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"components, each a slice of vertices in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, with an O(1) "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"component(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/components","title":"Components","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/stronglyConnectedComponents()":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/stronglyconnectedcomponents()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"}